From 259320839027ffc405a2460bc8824bafcb54154a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Arp: ratchet notes Ball, a ping-pong ball between plates that
 close in and part again

A roll over each half of the ratchet: the first half speeds up into its middle (each gap the one before times r,
r from the ratchet bounce as for the roll), where the ball buzzes at 15 ms, the second half is the same backwards.
With negative bounce the plates meet at both ends of the ratchet (on the step) and are furthest apart in its
middle. Bounce velocity Rise makes the buzz the loudest. Measured in Pettra "You Are The Seeds" (its synth stem,
separated with MDX-Net): the hits speed up from the beat to a buzz of about 15 ms and slow down again within the
ratchet. Menu Arpeggiator > Ratchet notes: Auto, 2 ... 8, Roll, Ball; saved as ratchetNotes="254" (older firmware
reads it as 8 notes).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
